═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 KEY FINDINGS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  1. Each m-row has at most 2 n-values (1 or 2)
  2. n ∈ (jm/k - 1, j(m+1)/k) — a Beatty-sequence structure
  3. Convergence is O(1/M) — same as diagonal case
  4. The 2D partition is NOT 2D — it's essentially 1D!
  5. For coprime j,k: the split m→{n,n+1} occurs at m≡0 (mod k/gcd)

  IMPLICATION: The off-diagonal proof may be much simpler than
  expected. The 2D piecewise partition reduces to a 1D sum with
  at most 2 terms per index, following a Farey/Beatty pattern.

